# client-custom-fields.collection.must-fail.patch
#
# Targets: FE-3034 AC "Cache key carries an object-type axis, byte-identical at
# default" — the DEFAULT half. The list key OMITS the `objectType` segment at
# the client default, so the default consumer's key hashes byte-identically to
# what it did before the axis existed (plan Correction 2, shipped AC-2) and the
# catalogue-scoped key every cache verb scopes onto still reaches its entry.
#
# Complementary control: client-custom-fields.catalogue-cache-key.must-fail.patch
# covers the OTHER half (the segment is PRESENT per catalogue, so two
# catalogues never collide). That one removes the segment where it must be
# present; this one adds it where it must be absent. Neither alone covers both
# halves of the AC.
#
# Authored by: developer seat (agent-seat-separation.companion.md — the seat
# that knows the exact line it changed authors the mutant; the prover applies
# it blind, confirms RED, then reverts — never reading src to construct it).
#
# Mutates: client-custom-fields.services.ts `loadList`'s `queryKey` — writes
# the resolved catalogue unconditionally instead of omitting it at the client
# default, so the default consumer's entry is keyed `objectType: "client"`.
# Sibling catalogues stay distinct under this mutant, so the collision
# assertions still hold; what falls is the DEFAULT entry's reachability — the
# key the cache verbs scope onto carries `objectType: undefined` at the
# default, which no longer partial-matches `objectType: "client"`, so
# `invalidate()` on the default consumer matches no query and re-reads nothing.
# `catalogueSegment` stays live, so the mutant compiles and the failure is
# behavioural, never a type error.
#
# Expected RED, both already on the branch:
#   - client-custom-fields.collection.int.test.ts — "AC-7 invalidate()
#     re-reads only this module's own key" (the default consumer's entry)
#   - client-custom-fields.catalogue-verb-isolation.int.test.ts — "AC-7
#     invalidating the client catalogue re-reads it and leaves the
#     cancellation-request catalogue alone"
#
# Expected GREEN, by design — this control is targeted, not blunt:
#   client-custom-fields.catalogue-cache-key.int.test.ts — the per-catalogue
#   collision assertions are untouched by a default-key-only mutation.
#
# Apply / verify / revert:
#   git apply <this file>
#   pnpm --filter @upmind-automation/headless exec vitest run --project integration \
#     client-custom-fields.collection client-custom-fields.catalogue-verb-isolation   # must go RED
#   git apply -R <this file>
#
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/client-custom-fields.services.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/client-custom-fields.services.ts
